son_slug":"sarah-hanson-young","vote":"no"},{"name":"Sarah Henderson","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10790","person_slug":"sarah-henderson","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sue Lines","party":"PRES","person_id":"tvfy_10782","person_slug":"sue-lines","vote":"no"},{"name":"Susan McDonald","party":"Nationals","person_id":"tvfy_10951","person_slug":"susan-mcdonald","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tammy Tyrrell","party":"Independent","person_id":"tvfy_11012","person_slug":"tammy-tyrrell","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tim Ayres","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10946","person_slug":"tim-ayres","vote":"no"},{"name":"Tony Sheldon","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10944","person_slug":"tony-sheldon","vote":"no"},{"name":"Varun Ghosh","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_11017","person_slug":"varun-ghosh","vote":"no"},{"name":"Wendy Askew","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10914","person_slug":"wendy-askew","vote":"aye"}],"name":"Committees — Adopting Artificial Intelligence (Ai) Select Committee; Appointment","noes":31,"question":"Anne Urquhart At the request of Senator Ayres, Senator Shoebridge and Senator David Pocock, I move: (1) That a select committee, to be known as the Select Committee on Adopting Artificial Intelligence (AI), be established to inquire into and report on the opportunities and impacts for Australia arising out of the uptake of AI technologies in Australia, including consideration of: (a) recent trends and opportunities in the development and adoption of AI technologies in Australia and overseas, in particular regarding generative AI; (b) risks and harms arising from the adoption of AI technologies, including bias, discrimination and error; (c) emerging international approaches to mitigating AI risks; (d) opportunities to adopt AI in ways that benefit citizens, the environment and/or economic growth, for example in health and climate management; (e) opportunities to foster a responsible AI industry in Australia; (f) potential threats to democracy and trust in institutions from generative AI; and (g) environmental impacts of AI technologies and opportunities for limiting and mitigating impacts. (2) That the committee present its final report on or before 19 September 2024. (3) That the committee consist of 6 senators, as follows: (a) two nominated by the Leader of the Government in the Senate; (b) two nominated by the Leader of the Opposition in the Senate; (c) one nominated by the Leader of the Australian Greens in the Senate; and (d) one nominated by minor party and independent senators. (4) That: (a) participating members may be appointed to the committee on the nomination of the Leader of the Government in the Senate, the Leader of the Opposition in the Senate or any minority party or independent senator; (b) participating members may participate in hearings of evidence and deliberations of the committee, and have all the rights of members of the committee, but may not vote on any questions before the committee; (c) a participating member shall be taken to be a member","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-senate-8821","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2024-03-26/10"}
